Not sure if this helps anyone, but I suddenly started getting this issue too. I had previously set the kotlin version in my `app.json` for `expo-build-properties` (to fix an issue a while back that I have long forgotten). Removing this then fixed the build issues I was having.

```json
[
    "expo-build-properties",
    {
        "android": {
            "kotlinVersion": "1.6.10",
        }
    },         
],
```

After reading all this, as of 5th April 2025 this worked for me:

## Step 1
Upgrade or downgrade to expo ```v52.0.36```


## Step 2
Install ```expo-build-properties```


## Step 3
Update your ```app.json``` to have **at least** this in your ```plugins```:

```json
{
  "expo": {
   ...
    "plugins": [
      [
        "expo-build-properties",
        {
          "android": {
            "kotlinVersion": "1.9.25"
          }
        }
      ]
   ...
    ],
```

After all that you should be able to build, at least I was.

Run
`npx expo-doctor@latest`

app.config.ts
`[
      'expo-build-properties',
      {
        android: {
          compileSdkVersion: 35,
          targetSdkVersion: 34,
          buildToolsVersion: '35.0.0',
          kotlinVersion: '1.9.25',
        },
      },
    ],`

This worked for me

I’m not exactly sure why, but moving expo-build-properties to the first position in the plugins array makes it work correctly.
```
{
  "expo": {
    // ... other expo settings ...
    "plugins": [
      [
        "expo-build-properties",
        {
          "android": {
            "compileSdkVersion": 35,
            "targetSdkVersion": 35,
            "buildToolsVersion": "35.0.0",
            "kotlinVersion": "1.9.25"
          },
          "ios": {
            "deploymentTarget": "15.1"
          }
        }
      ],
      // 그 외 다른 플러그인들…

    ]
  }
}
```
